{"parentUuid": "83771247-c8e5-4ae9-a5ec-1186ffa0d35a", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg4dnxbiCcn66s5AuMsVP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 709, "cache_read_input_tokens": 70813, "output_tokens": 467, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 64}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 709, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 467, "cache_read_input_tokens": 70813, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 709, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 709}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "type": "assistant", "uuid": "d8adfb6d-4022-400a-ac1e-ffc29a9a4f34", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T20:14:15.279Z", "userType": "external", "cwd": "/workspace/acme-web", "sessionId": "3468ea9c-8b44-46a6-b6ff-a84d1d45b2af", "version": "2.1.301", "gitBranch": "main"}
{"parentUuid": "d8adfb6d-4022-400a-ac1e-ffc29a9a4f34", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg4dnxbiCcn66s5AuMsVP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Jitter's in, and all 4 tests pass.\n\n**`src/retry.js`:** `backoff(attempt, jitter = false)` adds `Math.random() * 250` when `jitter` is true. The cap is applied after the jitter, so it never goes over 30000ms.\n\n**`test/retry.test.js`:** I kept your existing test and added three:\n- With jitter on, the cap still holds at 30s.\n- Jitter stays in the 0-250ms range. I mocked `Math.random` to 0 and to 0.999 so the test doesn't flake.\n- Leaving the argument off gives the old result, no jitter.\n\nHeads up on one tradeoff: because the cap comes last, once you hit 30s the jitter does nothing, and every client retries at exactly 30000ms. If the point of jitter is to stop clients retrying at the same moment, you'd want `min(base, 30000) + jitter` instead. Then it could go up to 30.25s, which bends \"keep the 30s cap\" a bit. I went with the literal reading. Easy to flip if you want the other one.\n\nAlso, jest isn't in `package.json`, so I ran it with `npx jest`. You might want to add it as a devDependency. Nothing's committed."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 709, "cache_read_input_tokens": 70813, "output_tokens": 467, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 64}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 709, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 467, "cache_read_input_tokens": 70813, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 709, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 709}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "type": "assistant", "uuid": "d7ad2cb3-7e87-497e-83c1-05d9c8a9472c", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T20:14:15.284Z", "userType": "external", "cwd": "/workspace/acme-web", "sessionId": "3468ea9c-8b44-46a6-b6ff-a84d1d45b2af", "version": "2.1.301", "gitBranch": "main"}
{"parentUuid": "3cc8f08e-9ccc-4ebe-9338-0d848406c7f0", "isSidechain": false, "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "nice. what's the worst-case delay now, with jitter on?"}, "uuid": "addaa139-fd3e-4070-9d6c-62f804058ae3", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T20:15:02.065Z", "userType": "external", "cwd": "/workspace/acme-web", "sessionId": "3468ea9c-8b44-46a6-b6ff-a84d1d45b2af", "version": "2.1.301", "gitBranch": "main"}
{"parentUuid": "53846c8f-6159-441e-8fdf-4a8380693d20", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg4dsW5fHX9Ks5LahmLB7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1090, "cache_read_input_tokens": 71522, "output_tokens": 388, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 127}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1090}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 388, "cache_read_input_tokens": 71522, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1090, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1090, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "type": "assistant", "uuid": "89ac15d0-0f8d-47fe-859a-81b861ac2b12", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T20:15:13.340Z", "userType": "external", "cwd": "/workspace/acme-web", "sessionId": "3468ea9c-8b44-46a6-b6ff-a84d1d45b2af", "version": "2.1.301", "gitBranch": "main"}
{"parentUuid": "89ac15d0-0f8d-47fe-859a-81b861ac2b12", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg4dsW5fHX9Ks5LahmLB7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "30 seconds flat. The cap is applied after the jitter is added, so nothing can go over 30000ms.\n\nHow it plays out by attempt:\n- **Attempts 0-4:** base delay plus up to 250ms. The biggest is attempt 4: 16000 + just under 250 = **~16.25s**. (`Math.random()` never actually returns 1, so jitter tops out just under 250.)\n- **Attempt 5 and up:** the base is 32000, already over the cap, so you get **exactly 30000** every time and the jitter disappears.\n\nSo it never goes past 30s. The catch is the same one from before: once retries hit the cap, every client waits exactly 30s. If you switched to cap-then-jitter, the worst case would be ~30.25s and the jitter would still spread retries out."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1090, "cache_read_input_tokens": 71522, "output_tokens": 388, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 127}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1090}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 388, "cache_read_input_tokens": 71522, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1090, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1090, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "type": "assistant", "uuid": "74a51476-682f-4427-97b1-d741ac40992e", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T20:15:15.906Z", "userType": "external", "cwd": "/workspace/acme-web", "sessionId": "3468ea9c-8b44-46a6-b6ff-a84d1d45b2af", "version": 